      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-4701",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=1 \\\\ y+z=-2 \\\\ -x+2y+z=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
